{
  "type": "doc",
  "content": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Kubernetes teams often use kubectl. I wanted to inspect settings with familiar commands rather than switch to a web screen every time."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "I tried "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "connecting to the lab cluster with Multi Agent and kubectl"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " and sent reads and modifications for the same ConfigMap to verify role-based control: reads allowed, changes denied."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Choosing a Read-Only Configuration Role"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "I used the existing "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Orders Lab Viewer"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " role, whose policy allows ConfigMap reads in acp-kac-lab/orders-lab. For "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "kac-fixture"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ", patch and update are explicitly denied."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Reviewing the policy confirmed separate resources/actions for Allow and Deny, scoped to an operator inspecting settings."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/kubectl-access-control/01.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 1. Reads allowed; patch/update denied on the lab configuration.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 1. Reads allowed; patch/update denied on the lab configuration."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Connecting kubectl with Agent Authentication"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "In Mac Multi Agent I opened "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Kubernetes"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " and chose Orders Lab Viewer. Manual Clusters showed acp-kac-lab, exposing permitted role and target as in the server exercises."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/kubectl-access-control/02.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 2. Read role and lab cluster in Multi Agent.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 2. Read role and lab cluster in Multi Agent."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The agent’s "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Setting → Kubernetes"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " documents kubeconfig paths and setup. kubeconfig tells kubectl its cluster and authentication method."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Using the agent-generated authentication settings, I prepared a separate "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "lab client.kubeconfig"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " with the local QueryPie proxy and qpctl authentication. Each command selected it with --kubeconfig."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/kubectl-access-control/03.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 3. Lab context and local QueryPie proxy address.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 3. Lab context and local QueryPie proxy address."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "localhost:16444 is this Mac lab’s QueryPie proxy, distinct from the Kubernetes API endpoint. With setup complete, familiar kubectl commands worked."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Reading ConfigMap as Usual"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "First I ran "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "kubectl get configmap"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " for orders-lab/kac-fixture. Name and data count appeared, and data.status was "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "READY"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/kubectl-access-control/04.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 4. kubectl reads the ConfigMap and its READY value.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 4. kubectl reads the ConfigMap and its READY value."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Normal output-format options also worked. No new command system was needed; the existing CLI now used QueryPie authentication and policy."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "A Change to the Same Resource Is Denied"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "I sent a request to change status to the lab-only EP44_CHANGE using "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "kubectl patch"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " against the same ConfigMap, not production settings."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The terminal returned "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Forbidden"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " with "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "“QueryPie - Denied by policy to access the resource.”"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ". Read access did not permit the role’s denied modification."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/kubectl-access-control/05.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 5. QueryPie policy rejects the ConfigMap change.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 5. QueryPie policy rejects the ConfigMap change."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "A new get showed status "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "READY"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " and resource version "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "559"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ", unchanged from before. Necessary reads continued."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/kubectl-access-control/06.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 6. Configuration and resource version remain unchanged.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 6. Configuration and resource version remain unchanged."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "I could delegate inspection while managing changes to the same resource separately through roles."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Auditing Requests Sent from kubectl"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Finally, I opened the administrator’s "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Audit → Request Audit"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ". The recent modification showed "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Event Type DENY"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " and Verb patch, alongside user, role, cluster, namespace, and ConfigMap."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Client Name was "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "kubectl/v1.36.1"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ", Request Source "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Third-Party Tool"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ". Request Body retained EP44_CHANGE."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/kubectl-access-control/07.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 7. kubectl change request retains role, target, denial reason, and body.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 7. kubectl change request retains role, target, denial reason, and body."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The subsequent read of the same ConfigMap by the same user/role was a "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "successful, ALLOW get request"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ", matching the terminal result."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/kubectl-access-control/08.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 8. Subsequent get recorded under the same role as ALLOW.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 8. Subsequent get recorded under the same role as ALLOW."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The convenience was "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "retaining kubectl while separating work scope and keeping history"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ". Operators keep the CLI; administrators trace who read or attempted changes, under which role, in QueryPie."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "This lab used QueryPie Community 11.6.7, Multi Agent, kubectl 1.36.1, and K3s 1.36.6 with test users and ConfigMap."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "References: "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
